 "about": "How a sale sent to CreateSalesRecords ends, case by case (SM-12; owner decisions SM-D1, SM-D2 in specs/shared-modules/decisions.md). Each case is something that happens to the request ('event') and what both apps must make of it. 'flow_error': the stage and status of the FlowError both flow interpreters raise when running sale.yaml (null: the flow itself succeeds and the reply check decides). 'outcome': not_sent (nothing was recorded for sure: safe to sell again), uncertain (it may have been recorded: check the state site first; the server's job ends 'rejected' or 'unknown' respectively) or recorded (with 'sale_number'). Run by mazama_sales/tests/state/test_write_outcomes.py (StateSession.create_sales + salejobs.proven_sale_number, and flowspec.run_flow) and mazama_mobile/test/write_outcomes_test.dart (runFlow + classifySaleFailure + looksLikeConfirmedSale). Event kinds a test turns into a fake transport failure: dns_failure, connect_refused, tls_failure (none of the request was written), timeout (no answer within timeout_seconds), reset_after_send (the connection was reset once the request had gone out), closed_before_headers (closed before the reply's status line); 'reply' is an answer with that status and body text. Failures that only one language can produce stay in that app's own tests.",
 "cases": [
